{"id": "feedback-zhe9hea5x3", "text": "Search works well for our group, and we are not asking you to change the interface or build automatic reporting. Our complaint concerns how the contract counts a search against our monthly allowance: reopening the same saved results consumes another paid search even when no new query is run. Please change that metering policy so reviewing an existing result does not incur another charge. The displayed usage matches the current rules."}
{"id": "feedback-mpfkmnhj7d", "text": "We assigned a user the documented read-only role and confirmed that the change was saved. That user can still modify project records through the ordinary interface, even after signing out and back in. Please fix enforcement of the existing role. We are not asking for a new permission model, clearer descriptions or cheaper seats; the current configuration should prevent the edits it explicitly says are forbidden."}
{"id": "feedback-rcq5w44gt6", "text": "We scan a supported barcode once, the device reports one successful read, but the inventory count sometimes rises by two. The published behavior is one quantity increment per accepted scan, and our logs show no second scan. Please fix duplicate counting in that existing path. We do not need a new barcode format, different confirmation colors or changes to the plan's item allowance."}
{"id": "feedback-nnne4u8axe", "text": "Our employees use the manual time tracker successfully. They now want a new option that starts a timer when they enter a chosen work location and stops it when they leave, which the product has never offered. Please add location-triggered tracking. A clearer manual start button would not replace this requested automation, and neither incorrect durations nor the subscription price is the issue we are raising."}
{"id": "feedback-vy7c4suybj", "text": "The invoice generator produces the right totals, tax lines and payment instructions. Our bookkeeper has trouble reviewing them quickly because the existing preview uses very little contrast between subtotal, tax and final amount. Please make those existing elements easier to distinguish. We are not asking you to add a tax calculation, repair a wrong total or change the price of the invoicing feature."}
{"id": "feedback-en6aznxc2j", "text": "The reminder system sends messages on schedule, and everyone receives the correct events. However, the settings describe intervals as offset one and offset two, so an administrator has to consult the manual to work out which reminder comes first. Please express these existing settings in ordinary calendar language and show the order more clearly. We do not want additional reminder channels or changes to the limits included in our plan."}
{"id": "feedback-h5q6xmgcw7", "text": "We like the existing version history and have no trouble locating an earlier draft. We need the same feature at its current functionality, but the extra retention fee is based on total workspace membership rather than on the three people who edit documents. Please change the pricing basis or offer a smaller history add-on. No saved version is missing, and we are not requesting any additional restoration or comparison tools."}
{"id": "feedback-peu34gknyr", "text": "Reminder delivery is accurate and timely, and the configuration makes sense. Our concern is the stated allowance: the plan counts a reminder sent to ten recipients as ten separately billed events, even when it is one shared meeting. That policy makes large volunteer groups expensive to operate. Please revise the recipient-based charging rule. We checked the invoice and it correctly follows the current rule; this is a policy request, not an accounting defect."}
{"id": "feedback-64an6nytxr", "text": "The invoice generator is documented to round each tax line according to the selected jurisdiction. With an ordinary supported invoice, its final total now differs from the sum of its displayed rounded lines. We reproduced this without discounts or foreign currencies. Please repair the calculation in the current invoicing function. We are not asking for a new accounting feature or lower subscription charges; the existing output is inconsistent."}
{"id": "feedback-d7hc7zf6q7", "text": "The inventory scanner reads supported barcodes accurately and updates quantities correctly. In a busy storeroom, the existing confirmation display is hard to distinguish from the screen waiting for another scan, so staff pause to inspect small text. Please make those two existing states more visually distinct. We are not requesting another barcode standard, an accuracy fix or more items in our subscription allowance."}
{"id": "feedback-m2pqf893dn", "text": "A reminder was configured for the morning before each inspection, and the activity screen confirms the correct schedule. The product's existing contract promises delivery at that time, but inspectors are receiving the messages after the inspection has ended. This also happens with newly created schedules, so it is not an obsolete configuration. Please repair delivery timing. We are satisfied with email as the channel and are not requesting an additional notification feature."}
{"id": "feedback-s228w9ub67", "text": "The available permission roles cover our needs and are enforced correctly. We need the existing audit-access role for external reviewers, but the terms charge those read-only reviewers the same price as full editors. Please offer a different price for that existing entitlement. The issue is commercial access to a capability that already works, not a request for another role or a report of unauthorized editing."}
{"id": "feedback-2nd2m5e2h8", "text": "The translation tool currently supports a fixed set of languages and works well for those languages. We need it to handle a newly required language with its own plural rules, which is absent from the supported list. Please add that language capability. The present review controls are convenient and existing translations are intact; our primary request cannot be met by a visual adjustment or a lower price."}
{"id": "feedback-t3trexhck3", "text": "The calendar's stated behavior is to prevent two confirmed appointments from occupying the same staff member's slot. Yesterday it confirmed overlapping bookings made through the normal web form, with both customers receiving valid confirmations. Please repair that existing conflict-prevention behavior. Our request is not for a new waiting-list feature or a simpler form; the current booking function must honor the availability it already shows."}
{"id": "feedback-fb9atnkmaq", "text": "Our files synchronize successfully and show the correct connection state. The current status icon is so small and similar in both states that staff overlook it before leaving a site with poor reception. Please make that existing status easier to notice and understand. We are not asking you to introduce offline editing, improve synchronization reliability or change plan access; we want the information already available to be communicated more clearly."}
{"id": "feedback-ms5rk7z48u", "text": "The calendar currently supports appointments at fixed times, and this behavior is reliable. We need customers to join a waiting list and receive an offered slot if someone cancels, but no waiting-list function exists. Please add that workflow. The present reschedule controls are understandable, and the subscription is affordable; neither a visual redesign nor a billing change would supply the missing capability."}
{"id": "feedback-nt7sags24e", "text": "Our invoices and their tax calculations are correct, and customers can read them easily. The concern is that your plan charges the same processing fee for a credit note as for a new invoice, even though the note reverses the earlier transaction. This is the stated pricing rule rather than an erroneous duplicate charge. Please revise that fee policy; no change to invoice generation or tax behavior is requested."}
{"id": "feedback-7xfam4by4w", "text": "The time tracking functionality fits our work and its totals are accurate. Contractors use the product for a few days each month, but the published billing terms require a full monthly seat charge even for that limited use. Please introduce an occasional-user rate or daily billing option. We are not asking you to develop a different timer, fix missing hours or change the way the controls look."}
{"id": "feedback-cu48ygpsfw", "text": "The board currently shows each project separately, which works as documented. Our delivery team needs a new combined view that displays dependencies between cards in different projects; no existing view supports those cross-project relationships. Please add that capability. We understand where the current views are located, and they preserve their cards correctly. The absence of this view, rather than navigation or pricing, is our concern."}
{"id": "feedback-jjsrfp66km", "text": "The current export gives us a spreadsheet and works as documented. Our publishing system requires a structured XML document with nested sections, which the product has never supported; renaming a spreadsheet would not help. Please add that export format. The extra manual conversion is inconvenient, but our primary request is a new output capability, not a rearrangement of the existing export button or a change to billing."}
{"id": "feedback-w85wk9kckn", "text": "Our surveys already support text and multiple-choice questions, and both work reliably. For a new study we need respondents to place points on an image, a question type that is not available. Please add image annotation questions. Making the existing branching controls clearer or lowering response charges would not meet this specific need, and no existing response data has been lost."}
{"id": "feedback-nd477ck3uc", "text": "The appointment calendar accurately represents availability and prevents conflicting bookings. Reception staff still need too many steps to reach the existing reschedule action because it is buried below less common account controls. Please make that current action easier to find and use. We do not need a new scheduling function or repairs to conflict detection; our request concerns the effort of performing a function that already works."}
{"id": "feedback-fnvtpc5xy6", "text": "Our translation workflow is reliable and supports every language we need. Your published policy charges for all words synchronized, even when a repeated synchronization contains no changed text. We want unchanged phrases excluded from billed volume or a plan designed for frequent synchronization. The meter is applying the policy correctly. Please change the commercial rule rather than adding translation features or investigating a content-loss defect."}
{"id": "feedback-3mxpjz6tn8", "text": "Our analysts can already search individual projects and the search is dependable. During quarterly reviews they need to save a query once and rerun it automatically every Monday, but scheduling saved searches is not a feature of this product. We understand that a manual rerun is possible. The request is to introduce scheduling, rather than shorten the existing manual workflow or reduce what we pay for it."}
{"id": "feedback-bs3j7wa3fc", "text": "The dashboard provides all the analysis our club needs and has been dependable. We want to share its existing read-only view with committee members, but the current published policy requires a full analytics seat for each viewer. Please offer a less expensive read-only entitlement or include viewers in the base plan. We are not asking you to develop sharing, which already exists, or to fix the underlying charts."}
{"id": "feedback-yqrtjq5mbv", "text": "The exported spreadsheets contain every column and the right values. We only export once a month, so staff forget where the existing download action is hidden among the account menus and follow an old training video each time. Please place the current export action beside the report and make its label recognizable. We are happy with the available file formats and are not asking for another integration or a different subscription."}
{"id": "feedback-268bwxsuca", "text": "All previous versions of our document are retained, with correct dates and content. Finding the right version is still laborious because the existing history panel presents every entry in identical tiny text and hides the author behind a hover action. Please make the current history easier to scan and compare visually. We do not need a new retention system, more storage or a lower price for the feature."}
{"id": "feedback-bkhh5ux3ww", "text": "Offline editing works for us during the trial, and it synchronizes correctly when we reconnect. The issue is that continued use requires moving every team member to the most expensive plan, even colleagues who never leave the office. Please let us purchase the existing offline entitlement for only the field staff. We are asking for a different commercial arrangement, not a new offline feature or a repair to synchronization."}
{"id": "feedback-gna6akbqxv", "text": "We can export the exact spreadsheet we need, and the service has generated it correctly every time. The current policy makes us buy a full additional seat for the colleague who downloads that file once a quarter, even though they do no other work in the product. Please offer a lower-priced viewer arrangement that includes the existing download privilege. We are requesting a change to plan entitlements, not a new file format."}
{"id": "feedback-mj34m7mpkj", "text": "The editor retains only the most recent document, exactly as your help page states. Our legal drafting process requires viewing earlier versions and restoring one when a negotiation takes a different direction. Please introduce document version history; we recognize this is a new capability rather than recovery of something the current product promises. Moving the save button or changing the subscription charge would not meet this request."}
{"id": "feedback-4gnzhrccy6", "text": "The appointment system works well, including its existing waiting list and reminders. We run seasonal clinics and need to suspend billing between operating months without losing our saved configuration. The current terms charge the full year continuously, and the invoices follow those terms correctly. Please offer a seasonal payment option. We are not requesting a new scheduling tool, a repair to stored data or another calendar view."}
{"id": "feedback-ew3ebers69", "text": "The survey service promises to save a response after the respondent sees the final confirmation page. Several valid submissions show that confirmation but never appear in the response table or export, even after the normal processing period. Please repair response persistence. We are not asking for an image annotation question, easier branching diagrams or a larger paid allowance; these submissions were within the existing limits."}
{"id": "feedback-b9uunfjp2k", "text": "We imported a valid spreadsheet through the supported contact importer. The preview displayed the telephone numbers correctly, but the saved contacts lost their leading country prefixes despite the documentation saying these fields are preserved as text. Please fix that transformation. This is an error in an existing supported operation, not a request for another import format, a clearer preview or a different billing policy."}
{"id": "feedback-2at59ftwky", "text": "The time tracker records the correct start and stop times, including work across midnight. Users accidentally open the existing edit dialog when they mean to stop a running timer because the controls share a similar shape and position. Please make those actions more distinguishable. We do not need an automatic timer, a repair to recorded durations or additional plan capacity; the current information and features are sufficient."}
{"id": "feedback-9jt9en2mmz", "text": "The invoicing tool reliably creates invoices in our home currency. We have begun working with overseas clients and need a new capability to issue an invoice in another currency while recording its exchange rate; the product does not currently support this. Please add multicurrency invoicing. The existing preview is understandable and our current calculations are correct, so a layout adjustment would not address the requirement."}
{"id": "feedback-ryw72k2anm", "text": "Contact imports preserve the data correctly and the mapping screen is easy to use. Our nonprofit regularly replaces a contact list instead of expanding it, but the published plan charges for every imported row, including replacements of existing contacts. Please change that usage policy to reflect net additions or provide a replacement allowance. The usage counter is following the current rules accurately; the rules themselves are what we want changed."}
{"id": "feedback-uwmdkpk3qy", "text": "Contact imports finish successfully and preserve the right names, phone numbers and consent fields. Staff have difficulty understanding the existing field-mapping screen because the source and destination headings look interchangeable. Please improve those headings and the visual direction of the mapping. We do not need another supported file type or changes to import accuracy; the underlying import already performs exactly the operation we want."}
{"id": "feedback-esaz7z9b5t", "text": "Invitations arrive correctly and people can join without errors. The sender's dialog places the final send action close to a nearly identical cancellation control, and several colleagues have abandoned a completed invitation by mistake. Please improve the labels and visual hierarchy of these existing controls. We understand how membership permissions work and do not need group invitations, another authentication method or a discount on the seats."}
{"id": "feedback-evkgfkxpkq", "text": "The contact importer accepts spreadsheets and does so reliably. Our partner provides address books in a specialized interchange format that is not currently accepted, so we must convert them manually before using the product. Please add direct support for that format. The field-mapping interface is clear and our allowance is sufficient; we need an additional import capability rather than a design change to the existing path."}
{"id": "feedback-8bab6fu9sg", "text": "The survey tool gathers and preserves responses correctly, and it already offers all the question types we need. Under the published terms, preview submissions from our own testing consume the same paid response allowance as research participants. Please exclude these internal previews or include a separate testing allowance. This is a request to change the metering policy, not a claim that the current counter is malfunctioning."}
{"id": "feedback-af3yrcp7c2", "text": "The translation interface preserves every approved phrase and shows the correct language. Reviewers spend time scrolling because the existing next-unreviewed action is at the bottom of a long panel instead of near the text they are reviewing. Please move or duplicate that current control in a more accessible position. We do not need another supported language, a repair to stored translations or a different charging scheme."}
{"id": "feedback-f3969jppn2", "text": "The dashboard promises to reflect completed jobs within five minutes, and that behavior used to work. It now keeps yesterday's totals for hours while the underlying job table shows today's completed work. Refreshing the browser does not help. Please restore the stated freshness of the existing metrics. We are not requesting new formulas, clearer chart labels or a larger allowance, and our volume remains within the plan limits."}
{"id": "feedback-ja79e5aa4b", "text": "Inventory scanning is dependable and covers all our barcode formats. The current plan charges by every historic item code, including products permanently removed from our catalog, so a small active stock still creates a large bill. Please base the allowance on active items or provide a way to stop billing retired codes. The current counter matches the published policy; our complaint is with that policy, not scanner behavior."}
{"id": "feedback-tk3eqhf6tn", "text": "We saved a search used by the audit team and successfully reopened it several times last week. Since yesterday, opening that same saved search silently substitutes another department's filters, so it gives us the wrong records. The controls themselves are understandable and the original data is still present. Please restore the documented behavior in which a saved search retains its selected filters; we do not need any new search options."}
{"id": "feedback-yvmnrpp44a", "text": "Our finance team selected all twelve months before exporting a report, and the on-screen table correctly displayed every month. The downloaded spreadsheet stops in September despite the documented promise to export the whole selected range. This is the same supported workflow we used successfully last quarter. Please fix the missing rows in that existing export; the location of the button, the subscription price and the offered file types are not the problem."}
{"id": "feedback-zuayd4vpc2", "text": "Email reminders are already available and meet their promised delivery times. Our field staff work inside a separate chat service throughout the day and want reminders delivered there as well; the product currently has no connection to that service. Please add that delivery channel. We are not reporting an email failure, and making the existing email settings more visible would not provide the capability we are asking for."}
{"id": "feedback-rdkuz23sed", "text": "The permission settings correctly allow and deny access according to our choices. Administrators hesitate when editing them because the existing role descriptions use nearly identical wording for materially different permissions. Please rewrite those descriptions so the consequences are easier to understand before saving. We are not requesting another role type, reporting an access-control failure or asking for a change to the plan that includes permissions."}
{"id": "feedback-8qwmj3jquq", "text": "The search engine returns exactly the documents we expect, including old archived projects, and we are satisfied with the plan price. The difficulty is teaching a new colleague which of the three similar filter controls narrows the current results. We keep opening the wrong dropdown and starting over. Please reorganize those existing controls and use clearer labels; we are not requesting a different search capability or a fix to result accuracy."}
{"id": "feedback-n2hq8nms4s", "text": "The board documentation says moving a card to another project preserves its checklist and attachments. The supported move action now transfers the card title but silently drops its checklist entries, even though attachments remain intact. Please fix preservation of that existing card content. We are not requesting a new cross-project view or a clearer menu; the current move operation is losing information it promises to retain."}
{"id": "feedback-dsmz66mery", "text": "The dashboard numbers agree with our source records and refresh when expected. New managers struggle because the existing legend uses abbreviations that are meaningful only after reading a separate glossary, and related controls are scattered across the page. Please improve the wording and arrangement of what is already shown. We do not need additional metrics, a different refresh mechanism or changes to the subscription price."}
{"id": "feedback-xcr4stu5b2", "text": "Our dashboard correctly displays all the standard metrics offered today. We also need a new calculation that combines planned workload with staff availability to estimate spare capacity, and no current metric provides that result. Please add this calculation. Improving the layout of the existing charts would be welcome in general, but it is not the request in this message; we need an additional analytical capability."}
{"id": "feedback-4nbw6xg7vt", "text": "The project boards work well and the cross-project view already meets our needs. Our clients only view their own delivery status, yet the current published terms require purchasing a full collaboration seat for each client. Please offer a cheaper external-viewer entitlement for that existing access. There is no problem with card movement or navigation, and we are not asking for a new client portal feature."}
{"id": "feedback-nmbvp5x3dy", "text": "The project board moves cards correctly and enforces the configured workflow. New team members miss the existing option to show archived work because it sits under an unrelated-looking workspace menu. Please make that current visibility control easier to discover from the board itself. We do not need a new archive capability, a repair to card storage or a discount on the project plan."}
{"id": "feedback-me35kpf5er", "text": "The product currently requires an internet connection for editing and clearly documents that limitation. Our survey teams spend hours without coverage and want to edit records locally, then synchronize when they return. Please add offline editing. We are not reporting lost work under an existing offline promise, and a more prominent connection icon would not satisfy the request. The problem is the absence of this capability, rather than its price."}
{"id": "feedback-kkayrdqwkc", "text": "Version history is included in our plan and promises to retain every saved revision. We can see entries for ordinary browser edits, but revisions made through the supported desktop editor disappear when that editor reconnects. The current document survives, so this is specifically missing historical content rather than a request to enable history. Please fix the retention behavior for that supported editing path; the history panel layout is clear enough."}
{"id": "feedback-pnjw3cqz3t", "text": "Offline editing is already supported and included in our account. Staff can save changes without a connection, but reconnecting sometimes replaces those changes with the older server version even though nobody else edited the record. This contradicts the documented synchronization behavior. Please fix that loss of saved work. We do not need an additional editing mode or different visual indicators, and our plan currently has enough storage."}
{"id": "feedback-5pqjb4nv39", "text": "At present, administrators can invite one person at a time, and those invitations work. We manage recurring classes and need to invite everyone on a saved roster in one operation, but there is no roster-based invitation capability. Please add it. Our primary need is that additional group operation rather than a clearer placement of the existing individual invite action or a repair to message delivery."}
{"id": "feedback-mdwrqrsm5w", "text": "The permission system offers workspace-wide roles and reliably enforces them. Our organization needs a new ability to grant access to only one project within a workspace, which is not currently supported. Please introduce project-scoped permissions. The existing role descriptions are understandable and work as promised; improving their wording or reducing the workspace price would not provide the missing scope of access."}
{"id": "feedback-bfdbgyfhqk", "text": "The inventory tool correctly handles the barcode formats on its supported list. A new supplier labels containers using a different two-dimensional format that the product cannot read today, and we need direct scanning of it. Please add that recognition capability. Existing scans are accurate and their screens are understandable; our request is not to repair a supported format or reduce the cost of scanning."}
{"id": "feedback-gsuvrf9x2x", "text": "The invitation screen says delivered, yet the recipients never receive the invitations. We tested several valid addresses at different providers and checked their spam folders; the same supported invitation workflow worked before this week's update. Please restore reliable delivery. We are not asking for a group invitation feature or changes to the dialog layout, and the billed number of members is currently correct."}
{"id": "feedback-5gug6x5khy", "text": "The invitation service works as described, including its clear note that pending invitations count toward paid membership immediately. That policy is the issue for us: many invited contractors never accept, but they still increase the bill during the waiting period. Please charge only after an invitation is accepted. We are not alleging a calculation bug, asking for another way to invite people or requesting changes to the screen."}
{"id": "feedback-eh7dvzbfbf", "text": "The survey builder saves questions and exports responses correctly. Researchers find it difficult to understand the existing branching controls because the arrows cross several unrelated sections and the condition labels are abbreviated. Please make that current branching configuration easier to read. We are not requesting a new question type, reporting missing responses or asking to change the fee for collecting them."}
{"id": "feedback-xc93u5e5jz", "text": "The existing time tracker promises to keep a running timer active while its browser tab is in the background. After the latest release it sometimes stops recording until the tab is visible again, leaving shorter durations than the actual work. Please restore the documented background behavior. We are not requesting a location-triggered timer or a simpler interface; we need the existing manual timer to measure elapsed time correctly."}
{"id": "feedback-3rg2hrwp8r", "text": "The translation tool allows an approved phrase to be locked against accidental changes. Several locked phrases reverted to earlier text during a routine synchronization, despite the lock remaining visibly enabled. Please repair the promised preservation of approved content. We are not asking for more languages or a faster review layout; this is a failure in a feature that our current plan already includes."}
